## Interface: 50504
## Title: |cff5fd7ffPanda|rQuest
## Notes: Quest helper and navigator for Mists of Pandaria Classic
## Notes-fiFI: Tehtäväapuri ja navigaattori Mists of Pandaria Classiciin
# The series only.  What ships is 0.2.<commits on this repository's main>, computed at package time
# and stamped into this file and into ## Title (build.py: release_version, stamp_toc); a third
# component written down here would be one nobody remembers to bump.
# 0.2 and not 0.1 because the counter changed meaning when the addon moved into its own repository:
# at the split (082c57d) this repository counted 84 commits and the platform repository 390, whose
# next build would therefore be 0.1.390, so keeping 0.1 would have published 0.1.84 against it --
# and the hub, which orders packages by int() on each component and offers the highest, would have
# gone on serving the other one.  README.md, "The version".
## Version: 0.2.0
## Author: vem882
## SavedVariables: PandaQuestDB, PandaQuestSync, PandaQuestAH, PandaQuestProf
## OptionalDeps: TomTom, Questie
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\PandaQuest\Textures\icon.tga
## X-Website: https://github.com/vem882/pandawow_addon
# Category is set because Questie sets it, and "Quests" is Questie's own value, so if the client
# does group by it a player with both installed finds them under one heading.  What 5.5.4 actually
# does with the field is NOT verified: the only AddOns-list source in the reference trees
# (Blizzard_AddOnList/Classic_AddonList.lua) builds one flat list from C_AddOns.GetAddOnInfo and
# never reads Category, and no Blizzard TOC in those trees declares it.
# X-Category stays beside it: nothing here reads it either, but it is the TOC's namespace for
# third-party metadata and dropping it would be silent.
## Category: Quests
## Category-fiFI: Tehtävät
